  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support To Local Humanitarian Entities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia Joint Response SomJR is a Dutch Relief Alliance DRA funded consortium of four Dutch organization (Oxfam Novib, Midair, SOS,and WVI) working with eight local partners to deliver humanitarian assistance to the affected population.
Out of the eight local partners, four of them are Nexus members, SADO, SSWC, working in South-Central and KAALO working in Puntland where three of them working with Oxfam and TAKOLU working with WVI in Somaliland.
The grant started in January 2022 and will continue till end of December 2023 where the consortium deliver assistance in the following sectors: Food Security and livelihoods, WaSH, Protection, Cash, Nutrition, Health, localization, and Accountability. With total budget of over nine million Euros.

Purpose:
- Support Nexus platform and promote the role of local humanitarian leadership of newly established entities
- Enhance the quality and timeliness of the implementation of SomJR activities and ensure mainstreaming and applying the concept of triple Nexusthrough the SomJR activities

Deliverables:
- Lead on meetings with SomJR Nexus members frequently and update Nexus members and steering committee about the progress and contribution of SomJR to improve Nexus performance
- Lead on developing and presenting innovative initiatives of implementing Triple Nexus concepts through the delivery of the SomJR activities
- Lead on organizing joint exchange/monitoring of activities implemented bythe SOMJR NEXUS members
Scope:
Timeframe: all the work and initiatives should be developed, implemented, and monitored during the project period which is between 01 January 2022 &#x2013; 31 December 2023
Organizations: Nexus will be leading and working closely with Nexus members ONLY participating in SomJR (TASCO, SADO, SSWC, KAALO) not all local partners within the consortium. At the same time, itshighly recommended to coordinate with other Nexus members which are not participating in SomJR (CPD, GREDO, WASDA, HAVOYOCO).
Funding: Nexus will be responsible of the coordination, monitoring and leading only, while the funding for the initiatives and implementation will be covered by members budget or JR budget.
Geographically: Nexus initiatives will be linked to members activities&#x2019; locations agreed under the consortium. However, SomJR is a flexible project and if there is a valid justification, locations can be changed</narrative>
  </description>
